## 1. Grammar

Replace the current grammar with:

```c3
const String LAMBDA_GRAMMAR = `
    term: <abstraction> | <application>;
    abstraction: ("λ" | "\\") <ident> "." <term>;
    application: <atom> <atom>*;
    atom: <ident> | "(" <term> ")" | <abstraction>;
    ident ["identifier"]: /[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/;
`;
```

This gives the intended associativity:

```text
f x y       → (f x) y
\x.x y      → \x.(x y)
(\x.x) y    → (\x.x) y
```

Wrap `LanguageCompileResult` in an owning parser object: compile once, deinitialize once. Remove the current module `init()` printing. A `ParseResult` owns its AST and text, so complete semantic lowering—and copy free-variable names—before calling `ParseResult.deinit()`.

## 2. Project-owned AST

Immediately lower to:

```text
Term :=
    BoundVar(index)
  | FreeVar(name)
  | Abstraction(body)
  | Application(function, argument)
```

Keep a stack of binder names while lowering.

```text
lower identifier(name):
    search binder stack from newest to oldest
    found at distance d → BoundVar(d)
    not found           → FreeVar(copy(name))

lower abstraction:
    read direct ident and body-term children
    push ident
    body = lower(body-term)
    pop ident
    return Abstraction(body)

lower application:
    collect its immediate atom children
    result = lower(first atom)
    for each remaining atom:
        result = Application(result, lower(atom))
    return result
```

For example:

```text
\x.x          → Abs(BoundVar(0))
\x.\y.x       → Abs(Abs(BoundVar(1)))
\x.\x.x       → Abs(Abs(BoundVar(0)))
\x.x y        → Abs(App(BoundVar(0), FreeVar("y")))
```

`mpc` inserts `sequence`, `many`, `string`, and `char` wrapper nodes. Use a helper that traverses these transparent wrappers and collects the first matching named-rule frontier. Do not use unrestricted `find_all_ast(application, "atom")`: it would also collect atoms inside nested applications.

