## 4. Destination-driven net lowering

Put this in a separate root-module `translate.c3`:

```text
emit(term, context_child_port, level, binder_stack)
```

Each binder state stores ordered occurrences:

```text
Occurrence {
    port: CHILD context port
    level: occurrence level
}
```

### Bound variable

```text
binder = binder_stack[len - 1 - index]
binder.occurrences.append({ context_child_port, level })
```

Allocate no variable node yet.

### Free variable

Create or reuse the named `FREE_VARIABLE` interface and connect:

```text
context CHILD ── interface PARENT
```

### Abstraction

```text
fan = new_fan(net, PARENT)

context CHILD ── fan.principal PARENT
fan.left CHILD  = body destination
fan.right PARENT = binder port
```

Then:

```text
push empty binder state
emit(body, fan.left, level, stack)
pop binder state
finish binder at fan.right
```

Finish the binder using:

```text
base_level = level + 1
delta[i] = occurrence[i].level - base_level
```

Cases:

```text
0 occurrences:
    connect binder PARENT to eraser principal CHILD

1 occurrence and delta == 0:
    connect binder PARENT directly to occurrence CHILD

otherwise:
    replicator = new_replicator(
        net,
        base_level,
        ordered_deltas,
        UNPAIRED,
        CHILD
    )
    connect binder PARENT to replicator principal CHILD
    connect each replicator auxiliary PARENT to occurrence CHILD
```

Under this level convention, `\x.x` has delta `-1`, so it uses a one-exit replicator rather than the direct-wire case.

### Application

```text
fan = new_fan(net, CHILD)

fan.left PARENT      = application result
fan.principal CHILD  = function destination
fan.right CHILD      = argument destination
```

Then:

```text
connect context CHILD to fan.left PARENT
emit(function, fan.principal, level, stack)
emit(argument, fan.right, level + 1, stack)
```

### Entry point

```text
root = new_interface(net, ROOT, "")  // port must be CHILD
emit(term, root.port, 0, empty_stack)
```

